Convert SVG into png.

	for i in *.svg; do inkscape -o 16/${i%.svg}.png --export-type=png -w 16 -h 16 $i; done
	for i in *.svg; do inkscape -o 16@2x/${i%.svg}.png --export-type=png -w 32 -h 32 -d 192 $i; done

Convert png into xpm.

	cd 16
	for i in *.png; do magick $i ${i%.png}.xpm; done
	cd 16@2x
	for i in *.png; do magick $i ${i%.png}.xpm; done

Scintilla only supports 1 character per pixel.

	grep '16 16' 16/*.xpm
	grep '32 32' 16@2x/*.xpm

For any XPM that has 2 or more characters per pixel:
1. Load into Krita
2. Filter > Map > Palettize...
3. Pick a palette
4. Save
